  "body": "Show sketches inside Labelore instead of a separate file server. `.planning/sketches/` is a GSD artifact folder like any other, so it belongs in the dashboard: a Sketches page built from sketches/MANIFEST.md (number, name, design question, winner, tags), each sketch's README.md rendered as a document page (question, intake, variants, winner), and a View button that opens the sketch itself, served read-only by the Labelore server at /sketches/<folder>/ from the target project. Every GSD project Labelore points at gets this for free. Want: the server serves only files under .planning/sketches/ (resolve the path, refuse anything that escapes it, no directory writes), and the sketch runs in an iframe with sandbox=\"allow-scripts\" and no allow-same-origin (sketches run their own JS and must not reach the app or its API). Open question: labelore.brkn.me targets ~/codebases/cinedise-portal, so labelore's own 28 sketches wouldn't show there — needs either a second instance aimed at ~/codebases/labelore or the multi-project targeting already named as a future direction. Open question: sketch data.js files embed other projects' planning text verbatim (027/028 carry duet and cinedise-portal todos and notes), so serving sketches publicly publishes that content — check whether labelore.brkn.me sits behind Cloudflare Access before exposing them. Today: sketches are reached through the ad-hoc python http.server on 127.0.0.1:4174 (-d .planning/sketches, does not survive reboot) plus a cloudflared quick tunnel with a random trycloudflare.com URL. Suggested interim: a user systemd unit for the 4174 server and a sketches.labelore.brkn.me ingress on the existing labelore tunnel.",
  "todos": [],
  "raw": "---\ndate: \"2026-10-23 03:11\"\npromoted: true\n---\n\nShow sketches inside Labelore instead of a separate file server. `.planning/sketches/` is a GSD artifact folder like any other, so it belongs in the dashboard: a Sketches page built from sketches/MANIFEST.md (number, name, design question, winner, tags), each sketch's README.md rendered as a document page (question, intake, variants, winner), and a View button that opens the sketch itself, served read-only by the Labelore server at /sketches/<folder>/ from the target project. Every GSD project Labelore points at gets this for free. Want: the server serves only files under .planning/sketches/ (resolve the path, refuse anything that escapes it, no directory writes), and the sketch runs in an iframe with sandbox=\"allow-scripts\" and no allow-same-origin (sketches run their own JS and must not reach the app or its API). Open question: labelore.brkn.me targets ~/codebases/cinedise-portal, so labelore's own 28 sketches wouldn't show there — needs either a second instance aimed at ~/codebases/labelore or the multi-project targeting already named as a future direction. Open question: sketch data.js files embed other projects' planning text verbatim (027/028 carry duet and cinedise-portal todos and notes), so serving sketches publicly publishes that content — check whether labelore.brkn.me sits behind Cloudflare Access before exposing them. Today: sketches are reached through the ad-hoc python http.server on 127.0.0.1:4174 (-d .planning/sketches, does not survive reboot) plus a cloudflared quick tunnel with a random trycloudflare.com URL. Suggested interim: a user systemd unit for the 4174 server and a sketches.labelore.brkn.me ingress on the existing labelore tunnel.\n"
